              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospitalisation of your 70-year-old male patient, admitted on 01/02/2021 with confirmed SARS-CoV-2 infection presenting as moderate-to-severe COVID-19 pneumonia. On admission, chest X-ray confirmed bilateral infiltrates, and arterial blood gas analysis revealed hypoxaemia. Blood tests showed elevated inflammatory markers. The patient was commenced on supplemental oxygen therapy, dexamethasone, and anticoagulation. Vital signs were monitored closely throughout. Remdesivir was administered over a five-day course. Physiotherapy was initiated to support respiratory recovery. The patient showed gradual clinical improvement and oxygen requirements decreased steadily. He is discharged in a recovering condition with oral medication and follow-up instructions. Please arrange outpatient review within two weeks. Do not hesitate to contact me should you require further information.</div>"
            },
